From 1a8e5ff3a86fc348b47c0527f145456ddea46baf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaci32u4 <lucaci32u4@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:22:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Preserve 'next' through account_login and honour it in
 the React login flow

The legacy account_login route redirected to the frontend and dropped the
query string, so views using LoginRequiredMixin (e.g. the django-oauth-toolkit
authorize view) lost their 'next' target. Pass the query string through and
make the login flow (password, SSO, already-logged-in) follow a same-origin
'next' path: via the router when inside the React app, via
window.location.assign otherwise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
